 then announced basically  so I I don't hold the voice the cabinet  responsible didn't stand up to Liz  Transit shoes she sat in the cabinet she  backed the plants well I mean the the  cabinet I think met literally three  times uh in its whole period so I think  trying to blame members of the cabinet  for what's happened over the past two  months is actually unfair just you know  for various reasons uh they they weren't  meeting you know for obvious reasons  given what else was happening uh in the  world but I think uh where we are now  then we need someone who who does share  the overall vision of a lower tax  smaller state but who recognizes the  reality that the most important thing is  to stabilize the economy uh to make sure  that Britain is a credible player in the  world again and Penny has already taken  steps she said she would leave Jeremy  Hunter's Chancellor I think that's a  very important step forward we've seen  that Jeremy with all his experience has  stabilized the pound stabilized the  guilts market so that is a very strong  message to send to the outside world in  the end although this is an internal  party election it's what happens in the  outside world that's going to decide on  the success of the next prime minister  and the next government and Penny's  already taken a significant step  forwards to that and it's interesting to  talk about Penny's pennymordans planned  because I guess the criticism that some  MPS have is they just don't know that  much about what her vision is about what  she stands for you know I remember the  last leadership election Ian Duncan  Smith telling me he doesn't know what  Paddy Morden has achieved in government  Lord froster when he worked with her she  wasn't always visible sometimes I didn't  even know where she was is she a bit of  a submarine yeah I think I think that  that last criticism is particularly  unfair and I can say that with some  Authority I was Secretary of State for  working pensions when Penny w